From: MedPlatform <noreply@medplatform.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] optee: STM32MP257F-DK, give the AFE hat's SPI6 to the Cortex-M33

The analogue front-end on the 40-pin header is driven by the Cortex-M33 on the
"amp" link, and in the ca35tdcid OSTL configuration every one of its resources
belongs to the Cortex-A35 (CID1). Reassign to CID2, non-secure, privileged:

  SPI6                     the bus (RIFSC 27); its kernel clock, FLEXGEN 18,
                           is already configured by this OP-TEE
  GPIOC 4, 7               SPI6 MISO, MOSI   (header pins 21, 19)
  GPIOF 7                  SPI6 SCK          (header pin 23)
  GPIOF 4                  chip select       (header pin 24, driven as GPIO)
  GPIOC 10                 PWDN              (header pin 29)
  GPIOH 8                  DRDY              (header pin 31)
  EXTI1 8                  DRDY's interrupt line

Checked on the running board before writing this: Linux claims none of the six
pins (pinctrl "UNCLAIMED") and uses EXTI1 lines 3, 4 and 5 only, so nothing
Linux drives loses a resource. Linux's own SPI6 node is "disabled" in this
devicetree; on the "spi" link it is Linux that needs SPI6, which is why this
patch is applied only when MED_EEG_LINK = "amp".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board/front-end specific configuration]

